    "description": "Join the Sankara Nethralaya family as a Senior Doctor in Kochi. We believe in empowering our employees with the tools, training, and environment they need to succeed.\n\nAbout Sankara Nethralaya:\nSankara Nethralaya is a leading organization in the Remote sector, committed to excellence, innovation, and employee growth. We offer a dynamic work environment where talent is recognized and rewarded.\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n• Participate in quality improvement initiatives and clinical audits\n• Conduct routine health assessments and screenings\n• Respond to medical emergencies and provide immediate care\n• Adhere to NABH/JCI accreditation standards\n• Ensure patient privacy and maintain confidentiality\n• Maintain sterile environments and follow infection control protocols\n• Monitor patient progress and adjust treatment plans accordingly\n\nRequired Skills & Qualifications:\n• CA / CMA / CFA certification\n• 0-1 years of relevant experience\n• Proficiency in Pharmacovigilance\n• Proficiency in BLS/ACLS\n• Proficiency in CPT Codes\n• Proficiency in Surgical Procedures\n• Proficiency in Telemedicine\n• Proficiency in Medical Ethics\n• Proficiency in Clinical Documentation\n• Proficiency in Medical Terminology\n\nWork Mode: Remote - Work from anywhere in India\n\nWhat We Offer:\n• Maternity and paternity leave\n• Company-sponsored certifications\n• Transportation and conveyance allowance\n• Employee stock options (ESOPs) for eligible roles\n• Comprehensive health insurance for self and family\n• Learning & development budget\n• Salary Range: 2.5 LPA - 6 LPA per annum\n\nLocation: Kochi, Kerala, India\n\nIf you are excited about this opportunity, apply now and take the next step in your career journey with Sankara Nethralaya!",
